#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
STAR TRACKER HUD - Optimized Edition
=====================================
Dual-render star tracker:
  - 128x64 1-bit render pushed to a physical SSD1309 OLED (SPI)
  - Desktop "Observatory Control" panel with a native hi-res sky view

Architecture, hardware pins, keybindings and catalog are IDENTICAL to the
previous version. Changes in this edition:

  FIXES
  - msg/calib timers were decremented twice per frame (once in each renderer)
    -> now decremented once in the main loop, so messages last as intended
  - desktop Moon used unbounded set_at() -> could crash near screen edges
    -> now blits a cached sprite (pygame clips automatically)
  - luma/PIL imports were mandatory -> now optional, so the script also runs
    on the dev machine (Windows/Mac) without OLED libraries installed
  - `import board` raises NotImplementedError (not ModuleNotFoundError) on
    desktop -> broadened exception guard

  PERFORMANCE
  - Moon sprites cached per (radius, phase, waxing) instead of ~600 sqrt +
    set_at calls per frame
  - text render cache (biggest win on the Pi: font.render was called
    ~40x/frame)
  - static desktop background (gradient) and glow sprites precomputed once

  AESTHETICS
  - desktop: gradient sky, soft glow on bright stars, diffraction spikes on
    the brightest ones, hardware status LEDs, UTC clock, live OLED preview
  - both views: real HORIZON line (alt = 0), shaft added to the off-screen
    target arrow
"""

